      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "likeCount": 5,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5d0516fa974f400f354eb85f",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 17
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I believe the system has needed an overhaul for a while now. There needs to be more information given to players on what the status is of an invite, a chat system of some sort to send messages like \"Hey sorry, busy,\" and over all there should be feedback in instances where the player is not the host of the world. \n\nBagel spoke briefly on jaded players, and honestly I've seen this first hand many times. Not being accepted and having no idea what's going on when you cast invite requests pushes some people's state of mind to bad places and they assume the worst case scenario, ultimately leaving the game for long period of times or turning bitter towards others who have established groups to join. \n\nThat's where hopefully more information might help keep people connected. The status update where you can display a short message and your availability was a huge step in the right direction, but it needs to go farther than that. People need to be able to see if the invite requests are timed out, not accepted, and people should get a message if they aren't the worlds host like friends only or invite worlds.\n\nThis in the end won't fix everything, but at least having more information in game will help direct people to what's going on instead of standing in a world wondering what will happen.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
