        "like": 8
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "There's a number of things that are leading to the game's steady decline. I'd say the biggest one is the lack of a \"game\" all vrchat is, is a social vr experience where the social aspect barely functions. I agree fixing the atrocity that is just sending someone an invite request would improve things dramatically but there are much more pressing things vrchat requires if it wants to maintain or even grow again. (like actual world scripting) (also lets not forget that it wasn't that long ago where people were totally unable to request invites from their friends at all)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "5d07b6096be00631081a586c",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5c590f0a028b3c4b40ee6c2c",
        "alias": "Interested Falcon",
        "aliasID": "65c332a3ed6eefce4c002dff",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/bd908491e1986ce4c8acd3ef2be1f848.png",
        "created": "2019-02-05T04:20:26.708Z",
        "name": "FuzzyFoxe",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "58c62efae9868f3662e9d9a1",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2019-06-17T15:47:21.367Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "likeCount": 4,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5d0516fa974f400f354eb85f",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 13
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "As much as this would help, I don't think they'll implement it anytime soon. It's not just lack of community cohesion, it's also poor developer decisions.\n\nLots of people are trying to find other places to go because of things like the unfair avatar rating system, or because of class warfare based on user titles.\nI've seen many streamers end up quitting either because of lack of viewers, or because of the constant wild and rampant crashing of either the game or someone using a crashing shader.\n\nFixing this would only be a small bandage in comparison to the gushing holes put in by the devs to \"fix\" other things.\n\nYou want an example of the devs -not- listening to community feedback? Look at the response by Tupper over at this request: https://vrchat.canny.io/feature-requests/p/adjust-volume-of-individuals\n\n\"We believe adjusting the volume of individuals isn't the best approach. We're looking into alternate spatialization systems (or adjusting the one we're already using) that should help solve this problem in an automatic and natural way.\"\n\nAbsolutely NO ONE wanted an automated system, but they're gonna do it anyway.\n\n865 people wanted a simple volume slider for individuals, but they're gonna automate it because the devs know what's best for the players somehow.\n\nIf someone manages to make a game that's better than Vrchat, I'll definitely switch to it. All they gotta do is listen to their player base more than the devs do here.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
