      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I believe that “9k to 5k” is a bit of an exaggerated and jaded stat. The game according to steam charts has had around a 5.5k players on average and the next spiked up to 7.1k January 2019, and now it’s just going back to it’s normal amount of average players, plus we now have the people that stopped playing through steam all together and switched to oculus, and the new players that play on oculus quest. So we are probably more accurately sitting at 6-7k players probably on average.\n\nI’m not saying the problem you’ve pointed out isn’t a problem, what I’m saying it isn’t a problem that causes players to just stop playing because of a quality of life fix. Do I want this part of the game to bug fixed? Yes. Do I think the game is dying like everyone else and their mother? No. We have the same amount of player base when started, actually we have more than what we started with if we exclude the boom of Jan 2018. The boom hit and we sat at 9k, then it calmed down to 5.5 to 6k, and we still have that amount of players if not more. Especially more dedicated players that stuck around all this time.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
