      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5b6b4e8cb1b04a6db0be465d|full_name}: But searching a party to talk to people and have discussions about topics is essentially what having a \"chat\" is about. Currently Public does not fit the criteria for the \"chat\" part. Too many cliques, memes and a extremely negative environment where you have to wade through hundreds if not thousands of individuals over and over jumping Pug worlds to find someone able to hold a normal conversation and most of the time these encounters are towards you and not the other way around. \n\nYou're right this isn't a MMO, Group Finders in MMO are anti-social tools, however if you put such a tool in a platform which is solely based around socialization. It would fare a lot better since right now many people feel left out from any meaningful encounters with individiuals solely based on the RNG of Public (And the Rank System..) and people want to conversate. But, they just don't have a tool to conversate about whatever they want right now with other individuals who want to conversate about the same thing.\n\nHence the group finder solution which would make it easy for anyone to jump into VRChat, create a group with what they want to talk about have people join them and just talk and meet new people who share their same interests or for people to check the group finder list for anything they might be interested in if they don't feel comfortable creating the group and what not. At the end the group simply disbands and vanishes after the group leader logs off or the group leader disbands it via a button in the UI.\n\nAgain read my comment again, public is extremely frustrating right now and the staff won't consider moderation changes to it. Group Finder would give them a easy solution so that people who dislike the randomness and wild west environment can side step it altogether and they won't have to do anything personnel wise to \"fix\" the platform.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
