  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-06-15T16:04:10.801Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Community cohesion is extremely important when it comes down to social games. One would argue that it is the second most important thing only being topped by security. If your game has a broken social system then the community cohesion won't last long.\n\nRight now in VRC if \"A\" person sends an invite to \"B\" person and they don't know why their invite is never answered it will create doubt thus undermining community cohesion. Rinse and repeat this a few times and suddenly you have a recipe for a jaded player who feels left out. \n\nYou have no idea what the friend is doing with the invite once they receive it. In some instances somebody can be blue status but be in a world that doesn't allow them to accept invites. This creates a situation where the game asks if you would like to notify the host of the room to invite them but we know that feature doesn't work. On top of that if you were to send a normal invite and it is declined it would make life easier knowing it was manually declined.\n\nThere is no reason a player should sit in a world and wonder where their invite is going for an hour. Having to take off their headset and DM a player hoping they notice the DM and await a response. Nothing has undermined community cohesion more than this exact moment.\n\nThat is the moment of doubt. It is the moment where you wonder if the people you hang out with has found new friends and has forgotten you. You fear the worst as people do and try to come to terms with this. This doubt in this moment can be fixed with a bit of transparency.\n\nIn the next update I hope to see this fixed. The system needs a complete overhaul to become more community driven and better to use. It isn't as simple as snapping your fingers and instantly having a better system I understand this. But regardless of work load this needs fixed for the community's sake.\n\nIf it isn't fixed there won't be much of a community left in the next year. On steam trends the game has been on a steady decline of actives users after January. Going from 9000 concurrent to over 5k. Hopefully we see a shift in growth soon brought about by better social features. Thank you for your time.",
